From 8b82d8262b73aa1485dffbde0fe8dc4cd06ce6cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthuchamy Kumar <muthucha@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:36:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] patch: fix code-review issues in DPP chirp/onboarding patch
 series
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses every issue raised by code review against the recent DPP
bSTA-onboarding/chirp changes (backhaul_manager.cpp, son_slave_thread.cpp,
ap_autoconfiguration_task.cpp, dpp_agent_task.cpp, bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp,
beerocks_event_loop_impl.cpp):

- backhaul_manager.h/.cpp: fix DPP bridge socket resource leak —
  m_dpp_bridge_delivered/m_dpp_1905_bridge_delivered now track whether each
  credential set has been forwarded to AgentDB, and
  process_dpp_bridge_events() closes m_dpp_bridge_socket and removes its
  event-loop handler once both sets are delivered, instead of leaving the
  wpa_supplicant event socket open indefinitely. Replace the hardcoded
  bSTAList AKM string in inject_dpp_bootstrap_key_and_conf_req() with a new
  bwl_security_to_bh_akm() helper that derives the AKM combo from the
  agent's actual configured backhaul security type
  (AgentDB::device_conf.back_radio.security_type), mirroring the
  controller-side wsc_auth_to_bh_akm() design. Fix a base64 decode padding
  bug in extract_net_role_from_connector(): EVP_DecodeBlock() always
  returns a length that is a multiple of 3 regardless of trailing '='
  padding, so the decoded length is now corrected for counted padding
  characters before use.

- ap_autoconfiguration_task.cpp: replace the hand-rolled DPP BSS
  Configuration Response JSON parsing's hardcoded magic-number offsets
  with an extract_quoted_field() lambda (offset derived from the search
  key's own length) and size()-derived offsets for the non-string fields,
  so the parsing can no longer silently drift if a key's text changes.
  Give base_auth_type a defensive default initializer — every branch of
  its resolving if/else-if chain already assigned it, but the bare
  declaration is fragile against a future branch that forgets to. Also
  drops the comment above the vap_label extraction line.

- dpp_agent_task.cpp: jwk_pubkey_to_der() hardcoded the "P-256" curve name
  and 32-byte x/y coordinate length regardless of the JWK's own "crv"
  field. Now reads "crv" from the JWK and derives both the OpenSSL group
  name and the coordinate length from it (P-256: 32, P-384: 48, P-521:
  66), defaulting to P-256 only when "crv" is absent.

- framework/platform/bpl/cfg/uci/bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp: dpp_connector/
  dpp_csign/dpp_netaccesskey were being derived unconditionally for every
  BSS, writing empty strings to UCI for non-DPP BSSes. Both occurrences
  now scope those three options inside the same
  WSC_AUTH_DPP-conditional as the sibling dpp/dpp_controller/
  dpp_configurator_connectivity options, explicitly clearing them for
  non-DPP BSSes instead of leaving them to be silently derived as empty.

- common/beerocks/bcl/source/beerocks_event_loop_impl.cpp:
  EventLoopImpl::register_handlers() now explicitly erases a detected-
  stale map entry before attempting epoll_ctl(ADD), restoring it only if
  the add fails with the fd still genuinely tracked by the kernel —
  cleans up stale bookkeeping left behind by a previous owner closing the
  fd directly, without risking corruption of a genuinely-active
  registration.

- son_slave_thread.cpp: move the anonymous namespace holding
  base64url_encode()/der_pubkey_to_jwk() (which uses the LOG macro) out
  from between two halves of the file's #include block into the
  "Local Module Functions" section where it belongs. Pure relocation, no
  logic change.
